    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268-a8">

                <pb facs="0486" n="476" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg476"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 10 in No. 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Tupper to Commander
                        Clarey.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Provincial Secretary’s Office,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Halifax, Nova Scotia,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 18, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I am commanded by his honor the
                    administrator of the government to acknowledge the receipt of your letter of
                    yesterday, explaining the object of your visit to be for the purpose of
                    delivering the steamer Chesapeake into the hands of the British authorities, or
                    to take her to the United States and deliver her to the United States
                    government, or to the owners, upon the faith, if any difficulty should arise, to
                    make restitution to the British authorities; and in reply I have it in command
                    to inform you that his honor is prepared to take legal charge of the steamship
                    Chesapeake, but cannot consent to her removal from this port until further
                    investigation by properly constituted authorities.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES TUPPER, <hi rendition="#italic">Provincial
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
